## FUNDAMENTALS

### What is Playwright?

```
Browser Automation Framework:
┌────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Test Scripts (JavaScript/Python)   │
└────────────┬───────────────────────┘
             │
             ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Playwright API                     │
│ - Browser control                  │
│ - Page interactions                │
│ - Network handling                 │
└────────────┬───────────────────────┘
             │
      ┌──────┴──────┬──────────┬──────────┐
      ▼             ▼          ▼          ▼
   Chrome      Firefox      Safari      Edge
   Browsers
```

**Definition:**
Playwright is an open-source Node.js library that provides a high-level API to automate Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit browsers over the DevTools Protocol and WebDriver BiDi protocols.

**Purpose:**
- ✓ Automated testing of web applications
- ✓ End-to-end testing
- ✓ Performance testing
- ✓ Accessibility testing
- ✓ Visual regression testing
- ✓ Web scraping (secondary use)

---

### Why Playwright?

```
Advantages Over Other Tools:

vs Selenium:
✓ Faster execution (event-driven)
✓ Better debugging tools
✓ Network interception built-in
✓ Auto-waiting for elements
✓ Better mobile support
✓ Multiple languages

vs Puppeteer:
✓ Multi-browser (Puppeteer: Chrome only)
✓ Better element waiting
✓ Built-in testing framework
✓ Better cross-platform support

vs Cypress:
✓ Multi-browser (Cypress: mostly Chrome)
✓ Better iFrame support
✓ Better mobile testing
✓ Can test same-origin and cross-origin
✓ Better network control
```

