### 2. Locators vs Elements

**Theory:**

```
LOCATORS (Recommended):
├─ Lazy evaluation
├─ Retried automatically
├─ Built-in waiting
├─ Better error messages
└─ Modern approach

ELEMENTS (Legacy):
├─ Immediate evaluation
├─ No automatic retry
├─ Need explicit waits
├─ Older approach
```

**Comparison:**

```javascript
// OLD WAY (Elements) - Flaky
const button = await page.$('button');
await button.click();

// NEW WAY (Locators) - Reliable
await page.locator('button').click();

// Why? Locators auto-wait and retry:
// 1. Wait for button to be attached
// 2. Wait for button to be visible
// 3. Wait for button to be enabled
// 4. THEN click
// All automatic!
```

---

### 3. Auto-Waiting

**Theory:**

```
Playwright automatically waits before performing actions:

Timeline:
─────────
T0: Action triggered
   │
   ├─ Wait for element attached to DOM
   ├─ Wait for element visible
   ├─ Wait for element enabled
   ├─ Wait for element in viewport
   └─ Wait for animations complete
   │
T1: Element ready, action performed
   │
T2: Result
```

**Example:**

```javascript
// No explicit waits needed!
// Playwright waits automatically:

await page.locator('button').click();
// Automatically:
// - Waits for button to exist
// - Waits for button to be visible
// - Waits for button to be clickable

// If timeout: Auto-retry up to 30s (default)
```

