## SELECTORS & NAVIGATION

### Selector Types

```
1. CSS Selectors
   Syntax: 'button.primary'
   Usage: page.locator('button.primary')
   Speed: Fast

2. XPath Selectors
   Syntax: '//button[@class="primary"]'
   Usage: page.locator('xpath=//button[@class="primary"]')
   Speed: Slower

3. Text Selectors
   Syntax: 'text=Click Me'
   Usage: page.locator('text=Click Me')
   Speed: Medium
   Use when: No good ID/class

4. Attribute Selectors
   Syntax: '[data-testid="submit"]'
   Usage: page.locator('[data-testid="submit"]')
   Speed: Fast
   Use when: data-testid available

5. Role-Based Selectors (Recommended for Accessibility)
   Syntax: 'role=button[name="Click"]'
   Usage: page.locator('role=button[name="Click"]')
   Speed: Medium
   Benefit: Tests actual user experience
```

**Best Practices:**

```
Priority Order (Best to Worst):

1. Test IDs (if available)
   ✓ Fast, reliable
   ✓ Survives UI changes
   └─ page.locator('[data-testid="submit"]')

2. Role + Name
   ✓ Accessible, user-focused
   ✓ Tests real user interaction
   └─ page.locator('role=button[name="Submit"]')

3. Text Content
   ✓ No special attributes
   ✓ What users see
   └─ page.locator('text=Submit')

4. CSS Selector
   ✓ Fallback
   ✓ Can be fragile
   └─ page.locator('.btn.submit')

5. XPath
   ✗ Avoid if possible
   ✗ Slow, hard to read
   └─ Last resort
```

