## PRACTICAL APPLICATION & PROCESSES

### Complete End-to-End Testing Workflow

```
PHASE 1: Test Planning & Strategy
─────────────────────────────────
1. Identify test scope
   - Features to test
   - User journeys
   - Edge cases
   
2. Define test scenarios
   - Happy path (normal usage)
   - Alternative flows (error cases)
   - Edge cases (boundary conditions)
   
3. Create test matrix
   Browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Safari
   Devices: Desktop, Mobile, Tablet
   OS: Windows, Mac, Linux

PHASE 2: Environment Setup
──────────────────────────
1. Install Playwright
   npm install @playwright/test

2. Install browsers
   npx playwright install

3. Create project structure
   ├── tests/
   ├── pages/
   ├── utils/
   ├── fixtures/
   └── playwright.config.js

4. Configure playwright.config.js
   - Base URL
   - Browsers
   - Timeouts
   - Screenshots/Videos

PHASE 3: Test Development
─────────────────────────
1. Create Page Objects
   - LoginPage
   - HomePage
   - CheckoutPage

2. Write test cases
   - Use AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert)
   - Clear test names
   - Single responsibility

3. Implement fixtures
   - Authentication
   - Database setup
   - API mocking

PHASE 4: Test Execution
──────────────────────
1. Run tests locally
   npx playwright test

2. Run specific browser
   npx playwright test --project=chromium

3. Run with debugging
   npx playwright test --debug

4. View HTML report
   npx playwright show-report

PHASE 5: Debugging & Analysis
─────────────────────────────
1. Review failed tests
   - Check error messages
   - Review screenshots
   - Watch video recording
   - Review trace files

2. Analyze root cause
   - Timing issues
   - Element not found
   - Unexpected navigation
   - Network issues

3. Fix test issues
   - Adjust locators
   - Add explicit waits if needed
   - Update expectations

PHASE 6: CI/CD Integration
──────────────────────────
1. Push to GitHub
2. GitHub Actions triggered
3. Tests run automatically
4. Report generated
5. Developers notified of failures
```

