### Q4: How Do You Handle Asynchronous Operations in Playwright?

**Theory:**
Playwright operations are asynchronous. Understanding async/await is critical.

**Answer:**
```
"Playwright operations return Promises and must be awaited.

// Always use await
await page.goto('https://example.com');
await page.locator('button').click();

// WRONG - No await
page.locator('button').click();  // ✗ Doesn't wait!

Async operations:
- Navigation (goto, click navigation links)
- Interactions (click, fill, select)
- Waiting (waitForSelector, waitForNavigation)
- Network (route, fetch)

Use Promise.all for parallel operations:

await Promise.all([
    page.waitForNavigation(),
    page.click('a[href=/new-page]')
]);

Use async/await for sequential:

const results = [];
for (const selector of selectors) {
    const text = await page.locator(selector).textContent();
    results.push(text);
}"
```

