## COMPREHENSIVE CONCEPTS WITH PRACTICAL EXAMPLES

### CONCEPT 1: Locators - The Foundation of Reliable Testing

**Theory:**
A locator is a way to find an element on the page. Locators are the most important concept in Playwright because they determine how reliable your tests are.

```
Locator vs Query:
┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ QUERY (Old Way)                          │
│ const element = await page.$('button')   │
│ - Immediate evaluation                   │
│ - Single point in time                   │
│ - Element can become stale               │
└──────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ LOCATOR (New Way)                        │
│ const button = page.locator('button')    │
│ - Lazy evaluation                        │
│ - Continuously updated                   │
│ - Never becomes stale                    │
│ - Auto-waits and retries                 │
└──────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Practical Example:**

```javascript
// ❌ AVOID: Query approach
const button = await page.$('button');
await button.click();  // May fail if element refreshed

// ✅ BEST: Locator approach
await page.locator('button').click();  // Always reliable

// Locator Chaining
const parent = page.locator('.container');
const button = parent.locator('button');
await button.click();

// Locator Filters
const list = page.locator('ul > li');
const secondItem = list.nth(1);
const lastItem = list.last();

// Locator with Text
await page.locator('button:has-text("Submit")').click();

// Locator with Role (Best for Accessibility)
await page.locator('role=button[name="Submit"]').click();

// Count Locators
const itemCount = await page.locator('li').count();
console.log(`Found ${itemCount} items`);

// Loop Through Locators
for (let i = 0; i < await page.locator('li').count(); i++) {
    const text = await page.locator('li').nth(i).textContent();
    console.log(text);
}

// Verify Locator Exists
const exists = await page.locator('[data-testid="status"]').isVisible();
if (exists) {
    console.log('Status element found');
}
```

