### CONCEPT 2: Auto-Waiting & Element Readiness

**Theory:**
Playwright automatically waits for elements to be ready before performing actions. This eliminates the need for manual `Thread.sleep()` or `waitForSelector()`.

```
Auto-Waiting Timeline:

Action Called:
│
├─ Wait for element to be attached to DOM (30s)
├─ Wait for element to be visible (30s)
├─ Wait for element to not be covered (30s)
├─ Wait for element to be stable (30s)
├─ Wait for element to be enabled (30s)
└─ Perform action

Default Timeout: 30 seconds (configurable)
```

**Practical Example:**

```javascript
// Theory: Playwright waits automatically

// Scenario 1: Modal appears after delay
test('Modal interaction', async ({ page }) => {
    // No need to wait for modal!
    // Playwright automatically waits
    await page.click('button:has-text("Open Modal")');
    await page.fill('input[name="name"]', 'John');
    await page.click('button:has-text("Save")');
    
    // Modal disappears, result shows
    await expect(page.locator('[data-testid="success"]'))
        .toContainText('Saved successfully');
});

// Scenario 2: Element is initially disabled
test('Disabled button becomes enabled', async ({ page }) => {
    const submitButton = page.locator('button[type="submit"]');
    
    // Button is initially disabled, Playwright waits for it
    await submitButton.click();  // Waits for enabled state
});

// Scenario 3: Network call completes
test('Data loads from API', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('/dashboard');
    
    // No need for explicit wait!
    // Playwright waits for list to appear
    const items = page.locator('[data-testid="item"]');
    const count = await items.count();
    
    expect(count).toBeGreaterThan(0);
});

// Custom Timeout
test('With custom timeout', async ({ page }) => {
    // Increase timeout for slow action
    await page.locator('button')
        .click({ timeout: 60000 });  // 60 seconds
});

// Force Wait Condition
test('Wait for custom condition', async ({ page }) => {
    // Wait for specific condition
    await page.waitForFunction(() => {
        return document.querySelectorAll('.item').length > 5;
    });
});

// Wait for Navigation
test('Wait for page navigation', async ({ page }) => {
    // Wait for navigation without timeout
    await Promise.all([
        page.waitForNavigation(),
        page.click('a')  // Link that navigates
    ]);
});
```

