### CONCEPT 9: Parallel & Sequential Execution

**Theory:**
Tests can run in parallel for speed or sequentially for controlled execution. Understanding when to use each is important.

```
Parallel Execution:
┌─────────────────────┐
│ Test 1 ├─ 5s       │
├─────────────────────┤
│ Test 2 ├─ 3s       │
├─────────────────────┤
│ Test 3 ├─ 4s       │
└─────────────────────┘
  Total: ~5s (fastest test wins)

Sequential Execution:
┌─────────────────────┐
│ Test 1 ├─ 5s       │
├─────────────────────┤
│ Test 2    ├─ 3s    │
├─────────────────────┤
│ Test 3       ├─ 4s │
└─────────────────────┘
  Total: 12s (sum of all)

Parallel is faster but requires isolation!
```

**Practical Example:**

```javascript
// Configuration for Parallel
export default defineConfig({
    fullyParallel: true,  // Enable parallel
    workers: 4,            // 4 workers
});

// Parallel by default
test.describe.parallel('Feature Suite', () => {
    test('Test 1', async ({ page }) => {
        await page.goto('https://example.com');
        // This runs in parallel
    });

    test('Test 2', async ({ page }) => {
        await page.goto('https://example.com');
        // This also runs in parallel
    });

    test('Test 3', async ({ page }) => {
        await page.goto('https://example.com');
        // This runs in parallel too
    });
});

// Sequential (for dependent tests)
test.describe.serial('Login Flow', () => {
    test('Step 1: Navigate to login', async ({ page }) => {
        await page.goto('/login');
        // Runs first
    });

    test('Step 2: Fill credentials', async ({ page }) => {
        // Depends on Step 1
    });

    test('Step 3: Submit form', async ({ page }) => {
        // Depends on Step 2
    });
});

// Mixed: Sequential within, Parallel between
test.describe.parallel('Multiple Flows', () => {
    test.describe.serial('User Registration', () => {
        test('Register user', async ({ page }) => { });
        test('Verify email', async ({ page }) => { });
    });

    test.describe.serial('Admin Login', () => {
        test('Admin login', async ({ page }) => { });
        test('Access dashboard', async ({ page }) => { });
    });

    // These two describe blocks run in parallel
    // But tests within each run sequentially
});

// Skip tests
test('Skip test conditionally', async ({ page }) => {
    test.skip(process.env.SKIP_SLOW, 'Skipping in CI');
    
    // Slow test
    await page.goto('https://example.com');
});

// Skip on specific browser
test('Browser-specific skip', async ({ page, browserName }) => {
    test.skip(browserName === 'webkit', 'Known issue in Safari');
    
    await page.goto('https://example.com');
});

// Run only specific test
test.only('Run this test only', async ({ page }) => {
    // Only this test runs (useful for debugging)
    await page.goto('https://example.com');
});

// Timeout configuration
test('Test with custom timeout', async ({ page }) => {
    test.setTimeout(60000);  // 60 second timeout
    
    await page.goto('https://example.com');
    // Lots of operations
});

// Retries for flaky tests
export default defineConfig({
    retries: 2,  // Retry failed tests twice
});

test('Flaky test with retry', async ({ page }) => {
    // If fails, automatically retried
    await page.goto('https://example.com');
});

// Retry specific test
test('Retry this one', async ({ page }) => {
    test.setTimeout(5000);
    test.retries(3);  // This test retried 3 times
    
    await page.goto('https://example.com');
});
```

